Manual test scripts
===================

These are the scripts used to test the modernize branch by running
the programs, as described in docs/NOTES.md ("Test recipes").  They
are not run by "make check": they need an X display (Xvfb will do),
xdotool and ImageMagick's import, and some need DOSBox, Wine or a
sanitizer build.  Output goes to ./manual-out/ unless OUT is set.

  play.sh PROGRAM [OPTIONS]...
      Play a level with scripted keys (walk, turn, shoot, doors,
      weapons, look, jump); report how it ended, UBSan reports and
      ASan reports.  GAME_DIR and WADS choose the data.

  netplay.sh PROGRAM NSLAVES [OPTIONS]...
      A master and NSLAVES slaves on one machine, on UDP ports 7777
      and up.  PROGRAM may be a wrapper that runs sdldumb.exe under
      Wine, to test the Winsock driver.

  dosbox.sh DIST [SECONDS] [OPTIONS]...
      Run DOSDUMB.EXE from dos/cross-build.sh's dist directory in
      DOSBox or DOSBox-X, walk, quit with Escape, show DUMB.LOG.

  xwad.sh PROGRAM MAP [STEP]...
      Open a map in XWad, enlarge the window, run mouse clicks, and
      take screenshots.

  noconsole.c
      A Windows launcher that starts a program without a console or
      standard handles, as Explorer does, to test sdldumb.exe's log
      file and message box under Wine.

A sanitizer build:

  mkdir san && cd san
  ../configure CFLAGS="-g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer \
       -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-sanitize=shift-base" \
     CXXFLAGS="(the same)" LDFLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined"
  make

shift-base is off because the fixed-point code shifts negative numbers
left everywhere, which GCC defines as two's complement.

Freedoom (https://freedoom.github.io/) is useful test data: put
freedoom1.wad as doom.wad, freedoom2.wad as doom2.wad, and DUMB's
doom/doom4dum.wad in one directory, and run with WADS= (empty).
